*~

# Generated trajectories and test outputs
*.traj
output*.json
convergence_*.png
benchmark_results.json
examples/*_controller.json
examples/*_stats.json
examples/test_*.json
examples/complex_mission_optimized*.json
# The generated mission exports. The two copies the robot needs live in
# pybricks_code/ and are tracked; a stray copy in examples/ is not.
examples/complex_mission.py
examples/complete_mission.py
complex_mission_optimized*
straight_controller.json
test_output*
random_suite/
benchmarks/
pybricks_code/hub_mission.py

# Research measurement output (the committed copy lives in docs/measurements/)
research/results/
research/missions/

# The mat pictures the studio fetches. FIRST's mat artwork is copyrighted,
# so it is downloaded on request and kept out of the repository.
mats/
# Calibration session artifacts. The studio writes them per robot, as
# calibration/<robot>.{session.csv,sheet.csv,poses.csv,sysid_fit.json}, so
# the folder is ignored rather than the bare names.
calibration/
session.csv
calibration_sheet.csv
calibration_sheet.html
poses.csv
hub_poses.csv
sysid_fit.json

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak

# The test cache: which tests passed, and the fingerprint of what they read.
# It is disposable - `python run_tests.py --clear-cache` throws it away.
.test_cache.json
